{"Negative offsets in OptimizedCursorPaginator allow accessing data outside authorized boundaries - Django querysets interpret negative indices as counting from the end, bypassing queryset filters and potentially exposing unauthorized audit logs": 0.6826817989349365, "Same negative offset vulnerability exists in BasePaginator - the comment claims underlying queryset will handle boundary conditions but Django querysets treat negative slices as reverse indexing from the end": 0.6364702582359314, "Redirect depth limit reduced from 10000 to 1000 (10x reduction) could cause incorrect assembly if span trees exceed 1000 levels": 0.8233211636543274, "Eviction strategy using zpopmin removes spans with lowest end_timestamp_precise (oldest), which may drop important early spans from traces": 0.8386595845222473}